      "refersTo": "message-user",
      "description": "A tonal message surface in the conversation panel.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-message\"><span>You</span><p>Create a launch page for Daylight.</p></div>",
      "css": ".ds-message{background:#14192d;color:#f3f4f6;border-radius:8px;padding:13px 15px;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-family:var(--font-inter),sans-serif}.ds-message>span{font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:#9ca3af}.ds-message p{font-size:13px;line-height:1.8;margin:7px 0 0;white-space:pre-wrap}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Page canvas",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "preview",
      "description": "The authored page is visually separate from its dark address chrome.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-preview\"><div class=\"ds-address\">Private draft</div><article class=\"ds-paper\"><h1>Good ideas deserve a place to grow.</h1><p>Introduce your next project with a considered, simple website.</p><section><h2>A little about you</h2><p>Your story, your work, and the details that make this yours.</p></section></article></div>",
      "css": ".ds-preview{overflow:hidden;border-radius:8px;background:#f6f5f0;box-shadow:0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.25);transition:opacity .2s ease-out}.ds-address{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:#171b26;border-bottom:1px solid #303446;min-height:39px;padding:0 12px;font-size:10px;color:#b9c0cf;font-family:var(--font-inter),sans-serif}.ds-paper{background:#f6f5f0;color:#182923;font:16px/1.65 Georgia,serif;padding:28px 7%;max-width:1100px;margin:auto}.ds-paper h1{font-size:clamp(38px,6vw,76px);font-weight:400;letter-spacing:-.04em;line-height:1.06;max-width:820px;margin:46px 0 28px;text-wrap:balance;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.ds-paper>p{font:18px/1.75 system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:680px;margin:0 0 62px;color:#41574c}.ds-paper section{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.35fr;gap:28px;padding:30px 0;border-top:1px solid #becbc0;border-bottom:1px solid #d9ddd4}.ds-paper h2{font-size:27px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:400;margin:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.ds-paper section p{font:15px/1.8 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#41574c;margin:0;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:500px){.ds-paper{padding-left:24px;padding-right:24px}.ds-paper h1{margin-top:24px}.ds-paper>p{font-size:16px;margin-bottom:36px}.ds-paper section{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:12px}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-preview{transition:none}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The GALX workspace and its page canvas",
    "overview": "This is a scoped extension of the incumbent [GALXAI design system](../../../DESIGN.md). Its authority is limited to the Sites component family, the `/sites` routes, and their linked [page preview renderer](../../lib/sites/site-preview.ts). The existing application navigation and global identity retain their own design authority.\n\nThe interface uses compact dark panels, clear text, restrained indigo actions and thin separators. A warm light page canvas gives the authored content a separate reading surface. This material distinction is already built; it does not establish a new palette for other GALX screens.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Compact dark controls with visible indigo interaction states.",
      "Conversation and authored page remain visually distinct.",
      "Serif page headings sit inside the preview; workspace headings use Inter.",
      "Loading, saved, unavailable and publication feedback remain readable in either mobile panel."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Canvas Boundary Rule",
        "body": "Paper and green ink identify authored content; workspace controls remain in the incumbent dark palette.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Labeled State Rule",
        "body": "Color never carries draft, live, pending or error meaning without readable text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Voices Rule",
        "body": "Inter belongs to the authoring controls; the serif hierarchy belongs to the authored page.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Quiet Depth Rule",
        "body": "Use borders and tone for interface grouping; reserve the soft canvas shadow for the page preview.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** preserve the existing GALX shell and indigo controls around the page canvas.",
      "**Do** keep authored-page paper and green ink inside the preview and its related content representations.",
      "**Do** preserve the left-conversation/right-preview arrangement on desktop and explicit panel switching on mobile.",
      "**Do** pair statuses with text, keep feedback visible in both mobile views, and distinguish loading from example content.",
      "**Do** preserve visible focus and reduced-motion behavior."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** turn the page template's serif typography or light palette into global workspace defaults.",
      "**Don't** treat a preview, saved draft or queued address as evidence that a page is publicly live.",
      "**Don't** add decorative kickers, glyph icons or hard block shadows to this workspace.",
      "**Don't** generalize local palette differences into detector exclusions for unrelated files."
    ]
  }
}
